{
  "name": "Start",
  "comment": "A call in parallel answers a task, and the next step runs before the called goal ends: Slow sleeps, then writes\n%order%; the step after the call writes it first, so right after, %order% is the caller's alone. (That the task\nthen ends with \"caller,task\" is read through `wait for` in stage 2, and in C# TaskTests.)",
  "step": [
